Reference: https://developer.close.com/api/resources/connected-accounts/get
## Authentication
- `Authorization` header (basic auth, required) — Use your API key as the username and leave the password empty.
- `Authorization` header (bearer token, required) — Bearer authentication of the form `Bearer <token>`, where token is your auth token.
## Request
### Path parameters
- `id` (string, required)
### Query parameters
- `_fields` (list of string, optional, default: ["_type","available_calendars","available_features","calendar_receive_status","calendly","date_created","default_identity","email","email_receive_status","enabled_features","has_meeting_creation_scopes","id","identities","imap","is_imap_archive_sync_enabled","label","latest_receive_error","latest_send_error","lead_suggestions_updated_at","organization_id","receive_status","send_status","smtp","sync_all_calendars","synced_calendars","user_id","zoom_account_plan"])

**SDK Code**
```python connected_accounts_get_example
import requests
url = "https://api.close.com/api/v1/connected_account/id/"
response = requests.get(url, auth=("<CLOSE_API_KEY>", ""))
print(response.json())
```
```javascript connected_accounts_get_example
const url = 'https://api.close.com/api/v1/connected_account/id/';
const credentials = btoa("<CLOSE_API_KEY>:");
const options = {method: 'GET', headers: {Authorization: `Basic ${credentials}`}};
try {
const response = await fetch(url, options);
const data = await response.json();
console.log(data);
} catch (error) {
console.error(error);
}
